##DESCRIPTION
##  Mental Math problems using compatible numbers
##ENDDESCRIPTION

##KEYWORDS('mental math', 'compatible numbers')

## DBsubject('Arithmetic')
## DBchapter('Integers')
## DBsection('Mental Math')
## Author('Peter Staab')
## Institution('Fitchburg State University')
## Date('5/3/2020')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',            'PGML.pl',
    'contextLimitedNumeric.pl', 'PGcourse.pl'
);

Context('LimitedNumeric');

$a1 = 100 + random(20, 30);
$a2 = random(10, 20);
$a3 = 200 + random(40, 60);
$a4 = 200 - $a1;

$b1   = random(4, 9);
$b2   = random(4, 9);
$ans2 = Compute(10 * $b1 * $b2);

$c1 = random(5, 25, 5);
$c2 = 40 * $c1;
$c3 = 40 + non_zero_random(-10, 10);

BEGIN_PGML

Answer the following addition problems using compatible numbers:

a. [`[$a1]+[$a2]+[$a3]+[$a4]=\;`] [__]{Compute($a1 + $a2 + $a3 + $a4)}
b. [`2 \times [$b1] \times [$b2] \times 5=\; `] [__]{Compute(10*$b1*$b2)}
c. [`[$c2] \times [$c3] \div 40=\; `] [__]{Compute($c1*$c3)}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
a) For this, noice that the 1st and 4th numbers add to 200. 
[```[$a1]+[$a2]+[$a3]+[$a4]= ([$a1]+[$a4]) + ([$a2]+[$a3]) = 200 + [$a2+$a3] = [$a1+$a2+$a3+$a4]```]
b) Rearrange this to make the calculation easier.
[``` 2 \times [$b1] \times [$b2] \times 5= (2 \times 5) \times ([$b1]\times[$b2]) =
    10 \times [$b1*$b2] = [$b1*$b2*10] ```]
c) Again, rearrange makes this easier.
[``` [$c2] \times [$c3] \div 40 = ([$c2] \div 40) \times [$c3] = [$c2/40] \times [$c3] = [$c1*$c3]```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();
